Parse every frame without reconstructing or filtering it.

The decoder parses each superblock with decode_partition()'s parse-only flag
(0x1) through the single superblock coding block buffer, and hands each
transform block and each coding block to the WebGPU Player parser bridge,
which writes them into the frame's GPU record and clears the coefficients.
Prediction, reconstruction, the monochrome neutral chroma, deblocking, CDEF,
super-resolution, and loop restoration are skipped; the compute shaders run
them. Super-resolution keeps the frame buffer's upscaled geometry, so later
frames see the reference's upscaled size, and a reference lost in error
resilient mode goes to the bridge instead of being filled with grey, which
leaves set_planes_to_neutral_grey() unused, so it goes.
Everything later frames' parsing reads is kept: motion vectors, segment ids,
CDFs, global motion, and the reference map.

